# selftests.list: Linux's KVM selftests in the KVM suite, one a line: the
# program's path under /opt/kvm-selftests, what corpus.sh requires of it under
# Rach2's KVM, Linux's result on the testing PC, and the reason. EXPECT is
# `pass`, an exit of 0; `skip`, the kselftest skip, exit 4, for what the
# processor lacks, as Linux skips it there; `fail`, another exit, where Linux
# fails and Rach2 is to fail as it does; or `excluded`, not run, for one of
# the reasons the stack's approved plan allows. A test whose result is the
# processor's has FLAG?A:B there: A on a processor whose `flags` in
# /proc/cpuinfo have FLAG, or whose KVM answers KVM_CAP_VM_TSC_CONTROL where
# FLAG is `kvm_cap_vm_tsc_control`, and B on one without it. LINUX is the
# result of the same 6.12.115 programs under Linux 6.18.58, WSL's, as
# ref/linux-selftests.status has it; a row Linux failed there, where the
# programs are older than the kernel, expects a pass unless its EXPECT is
# `fail`, and names Linux's failure after `Linux:`. A NAME PROGRAM,ARG,...
# runs PROGRAM with the ARGs: the six programs that touch a gigabyte or more
# at their defaults run at smaller sizes, since the suite's guests run them
# two hypervisors deep, where Linux as the host took 484 s for
# max_guest_memory_test at 4 GiB and would take hours at its 128 GiB
# (dev-log/84-locks/84-33.md). Inside a machine of KVM, as the KVM suite's
# cases run, FLAG `outer_kvm` holds: there x86_64/apic_bus_clock_test and
# x86_64/hyperv_clock are excluded and memslot_perf_test and
# x86_64/fix_hypercall_test fail, as under Linux 6.12 as the host of the same
# machine. Under another hypervisor, as under the Mac's TCG, which etude gives
# one processor, rseq_test skips and x86_64/debug_regs fails, as Linux does
# there by the two codes (dev-log/84-locks/84-239.md). A test is expected to
# fail only where Linux as the host of the same machine fails it, and its
# row names how.
#
# NAME EXPECT LINUX REASON
access_tracking_perf_test skip skip CONFIG_IDLE_PAGE_TRACKING is not enabled
coalesced_io_test pass pass
demand_paging_test,-b,64M pass pass
dirty_log_perf_test,-b,64M pass pass
dirty_log_test,-i,4 pass fail Linux: Set page 369 value 1 incorrect (iteration=3)
guest_memfd_test excluded fail guest_memfd, deferred by the owner's decision of 2026-11-10 to a later milestone; Linux: guest_memfd() with flag '0x1' should fail with EINVAL
guest_print_test pass pass
hardware_disable_test pass pass
kvm_binary_stats_test pass pass
kvm_create_max_vcpus pass pass
kvm_page_table_test,-b,128M pass pass
max_guest_memory_test,-m,4 pass pass built with vendor/gnu/kvm/max-guest-memory-one-cpu.patch, without which its default of no vCPUs on one processor, as an SVM profile under TCG has, stops it before -c is read
memslot_modification_stress_test,-b,64M pass pass
memslot_perf_test outer_kvm?fail:pass pass inside a machine of KVM, its RW case's first write of each page is a nested exit, so that a pass outlasts host_perform_sync's alarm(10) (memslot_perf_test.c:418-426), as under Linux 6.12 as the host of the same machine (dev-log/84-locks/84-33.md)
pre_fault_memory_test pass pass
rseq_test outer_kvm?pass:hypervisor?skip:pass pass under another hypervisor, as under the Mac's TCG, where etude gives the machine one processor, skips for want of CPU_COUNT(&possible_mask) >= 2, as Linux does on one processor (dev-log/84-locks/84-239.md)
set_memory_region_test pass fail Linux: Unexpected exit mmio address = 0x180000
steal_time pass pass
system_counter_offset_test pass pass
x86_64/amx_test skip skip Required XSAVE feature 'XFEATURE_MASK_XTILE_DATA' not supported
x86_64/apic_bus_clock_test outer_kvm?excluded:pass pass not run inside a machine of KVM, where the outer host's scheduling decides it: it compares the guest's TSC with KVM's clock across exits, and with the testing PC loaded Linux 6.12 as the KVM host of the same machine failed it 2 times in 280 runs of it and hyperv_clock, and Rach2 5 (dev-log/84-locks/84-33.md)
x86_64/cpuid_test pass pass
x86_64/cr4_cpuid_sync_test pass pass
x86_64/debug_regs outer_kvm?pass:hypervisor?fail:pass pass under another hypervisor, as under the Mac's TCG, fails at sw_bp, where the guest takes its own #BP: TCG checks INT3 against the INTn intercept and not against the #BP intercept that KVM_GUESTDBG_USE_SW_BP sets, under Linux's KVM as under Rach2's (dev-log/84-locks/84-239.md)
x86_64/dirty_log_page_splitting_test skip skip HUGETLB is not enabled in /proc/sys/vm/nr_hugepages
x86_64/exit_on_emulation_failure_test pass pass
x86_64/fix_hypercall_test outer_kvm?fail:pass pass under Linux's KVM beneath, that KVM takes the nested guest's #UD itself and writes VMMCALL over its VMCALL (Linux arch/x86/kvm/svm/nested.c:1540-1545, x86.c:9729-9738), so that disable_quirk's hypercall succeeds at fix_hypercall_test.c:75, as under Linux at the same depth
x86_64/get_msr_index_features pass pass
x86_64/hwcr_msr_test pass pass
x86_64/hyperv_clock outer_kvm?excluded:pass pass not run inside a machine of KVM, where the outer host's scheduling decides it: it compares the guest's TSC with KVM's clock across exits, and with the testing PC loaded Linux 6.12 as the KVM host of the same machine failed it 2 times in 280 runs of it and apic_bus_clock_test, and Rach2 5 (dev-log/84-locks/84-33.md)
x86_64/hyperv_cpuid pass pass
x86_64/hyperv_evmcs skip skip Requirement not met: kvm_cpu_has(X86_FEATURE_VMX)
x86_64/hyperv_extended_hypercalls pass pass
x86_64/hyperv_features pass pass
x86_64/hyperv_ipi pass pass
x86_64/hyperv_svm_test excluded pass nested virtualization, excluded by the owner's decision of 2026-11-10: Rach2's KVM gives its guests neither SVM nor VMX, which the test's nested half needs
x86_64/hyperv_tlb_flush pass pass
x86_64/kvm_clock_test pass pass
x86_64/kvm_pv_test pass fail Linux: KVM_ENABLE_CAP failed, rc: -1 errno: 22 (Invalid argument)
x86_64/max_vcpuid_cap_test pass pass
x86_64/monitor_mwait_test monitor?fail:skip skip Requirement not met: this_cpu_has(X86_FEATURE_MWAIT), as on the testing PC under Hyper-V; with MONITOR and MWAIT the program asks KVM_CAP_DISABLE_QUIRKS2 to turn a quirk back on, which Linux 6.12.115 does not do, and by their sources fails there at its third case
x86_64/nested_exceptions_test excluded pass nested virtualization, excluded by the owner's decision of 2026-11-10: Rach2's KVM gives its guests neither SVM nor VMX
x86_64/nx_huge_pages_test skip skip Running via nx_huge_pages_test.sh, which also handles environment setup, is strongly recommended.
x86_64/platform_info_test pass fail Linux: KVM_SET_MSRS failed on MSR_PLATFORM_INFO, value = 0x80000000
x86_64/pmu_counters_test intel?kvm_pmu?pass:skip:skip skip Requirement not met: host_cpu_is_intel; Intel's PMU runs it
x86_64/pmu_event_filter_test kvm_pmu?pass:skip pass Guest event filters; skips without a host PMU
x86_64/private_mem_conversions_test skip skip Requirement not met: kvm_check_cap(KVM_CAP_VM_TYPES) & BIT(KVM_X86_SW_PROTECTED_VM)
x86_64/private_mem_kvm_exits_test skip skip Requirement not met: kvm_check_cap(KVM_CAP_VM_TYPES) & BIT(KVM_X86_SW_PROTECTED_VM)
